Z||000025||grgoyl86||12-23-2001||09:18 PM||||Ski - do you have a higher-res version of this one? I'd like to do a test print. I can do these on 24x36, and I think I can do it for $10 or less. Would that be a worthwhile price?<P>If you have a higher-res version, send it to me at bobschlag@fieropride.com<P>Bob||||reg||1
Z||000026||MinnGreenGT||12-23-2001||10:03 PM||||Well, I go away for a day or two and see what I miss!?!?<P>Anyway- for those of you who didn't read the thread cooter listed above.  I run a company, <A HREF="http://www.romatekgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>Romatek Graphics</A> (I know, not much of a website yet...but I'm working on it).  Anyway, I'm running an 8-color Wide format printer (<A HREF="http://www.encad.com" TARGET=_blank>Encad 850</A>)- capabable of running 48"+ wide prints (up to 60" wide media if necessary- 50" is standard).  We normally specialize in photo-quality reproductions for trade show displays and POP use.  I have offered this a few times before... but never got much of a response.  I was asking $50 for custom 2'x3' prints on semi-gloss paper, and $10 more for laminated prints (for better durability).  I am currently doing finishing touches on an LT1 ChopTop poster that I was going to use a promo bit to show to "the forum". Of course that image is at my office- and I'm not headed over there for a couple of days (maybe Tues if necessary).  I was photoshopping his image to get something in this style for starters:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/f355poster.jpg"> <P>I will certainly offer a volume discount (SkiTime- I got your email). Say to $30 if you can get 10 or more ordered.  Does that sound reasonable?  (BTW: My price includes basic shipping). I can't really go much lower because I have to cover production costs of the high quality paper and 8 separate color cartridges (these things are $145ea to replace btw).<P>The $50 price for custom pieces would include high-resolution scanning of a printed photo if necessary.  Any photoshopping (beyond adding a tagline with your name/year/car/model) would be extra.  And for those wishing to submit digitl files... depends on the quality of the photo.  Minimum target resolution is 100 pixels per inch at full printed size (that's 2400x3600 pixels for a 2'x3' poster). If you can scan higher- great. If not... it may not reproduce quite like a photo at such a magnification (realize that professional posters are usually shot with a 3x5 negative or larger- standard 35mm cameras are only about 1x1.5 negatives).<P>I will try to check this thread again later... but no guarantees on timing.  Please email me directly at  <A HREF="mailto:MacGod911@aol.com">MacGod911@aol.com</A>  for now if you want specific info! Thanks for the interest.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000027||kempo||12-24-2001||02:14 AM||||MinnGreen- as said, I'll be the first to order, so then you'll need 9 more!  ||||reg||1
Z||000028||FieroLisa||12-24-2001||02:17 AM||||Hmmmmmmm I want the kick A$$ poster of my car that Reality drew up there, but even more so the poster of Skitime's car.... *droooooool* gee, glad I got the chance to drive that baby!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif">                 <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A> *<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa1/showdates.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Events 2002</A> *<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tarheel Fieros</A>||||reg||1
Z||000029||MinnGreenGT||12-24-2001||10:36 AM||||Just a couple more notes.  <P>First about resolution and filesize. I regularily can blow up 2.5MP digital camera files to the 2'x3' size and they work well. But for superior photo quality a finished photoshop file (without extra "special effects") can easily pass the 50MB mark (it is not unusual for my larger multi-panel project files to exceed 500+MB).  Basically what I'm trying to say is that the output quality is really dependant on the input quality (the machine outputs 600+dpi, but input is normally only 100-150 pix/in for large displays).<P>And about pricing. I know I'm listing a higher base price than grgoyl86, but I am running a very expensive new 8 color printing system that does run a higher cost per sq/ft. I am running a full set of high-grade inks (supposed to last without fading for nearly 25 years if placed under glass) and paper. And the Encad systems produce the most brilliant reds and blues available (originally purchased a MacDermod/Colorspan that couldn't hit a bright red if it's life depended on it-and it did <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).  But I can print on just about anything if you need it! I can even produce things on an artist canvas if someone is looking for a really high quality, more artistic appearance.<P>Anyway I'm just trying to add a little more info to help people understand the system!<P>Merry Christmas everyone!!!||||reg||1
Z||000030||RossT||12-24-2001||10:50 AM||||Here are a few that I have on the wall:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image001_2.jpg"> <P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Image003_3.jpg"> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000031||Patrick's Dad||12-24-2001||11:51 AM||||I hate to throw water on some of this (not all), but the dreaded "C" word enters into this discussion: Copyright.<P>For the factory images and some of the other artwork represented to be reproduced requires written permission of the publisher and/or artist.<P>For the images of cars that are owned by forum members, I would still advise a contract with the printers, even a boilerplate, just to protect all parties. As a Fiero owner, I'd love to get a great image, but as a photographer, I'd hate to get my work ripped off.<P>I'd been thinking over the last couple of weeks that I'd like a nice, high quality print, maybe modeled after the Pirelli or Snap-On calendars....||||reg||1
Z||000032||Joe Torma||12-24-2001||12:52 PM||||I agree with the above post.<P>I'm going to go ahead with my mini-posters and have contacted a few members so far and offered "royalties" to them.  <P>For big posters you should see MinnGreen or grgoyle86||||reg||1
