Z||000036||FieroMontreal||12-24-2001||04:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by yo_sweet:<BR><B>ill take one of my car thanks<P><BR>after all mines faster better, pics up chicks better then all posted above <P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You talking about that Fire Chicken? Pfft.. the only thing you can pick up in that thing are cheap hookers!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontrealholidays.gif"> <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000037||MinnGreenGT||12-24-2001||05:31 PM||||I agree with Patrick's Dad (hmmm... that sounds funny to say it like that <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).  Copyright is VERY important. And I certainly will not be reproducing any existing artowrk/posters/etc... without explicit permission from the artist/manufacturer.<P>As to any agreements with personal photos- I feel equally strong about that.  I would be royally ticked off if someone used one of my photographs without my permission- and especially without giving recognition to the owner/photographer.  On LT1 ChopTop's poster that I'm working on, it has the "copyright" listed to the owners name.  And I intend to do the same with anyone's photos who I reproduce. If anyone happens to have a contract handy, or knows the correct language to write one... I'd be glad to sign it for every project I do!  Just don't ask me to copy any type of professional photo/art/advertisment unless you are the creator.<P>Also, I will not sell you a copy of someone else's poster without their permission.  And maybe that should be included in the contract- for every copy of ______'s poster I sell, ______ will recieve a comission/royalty of $_.__<P>Just another suggestion!  And keep it up- it's good to make sure everyone is aware of all aspects of print/production.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000038||The Fieromaster||12-24-2001||05:37 PM||||MinnGreen thinkin on your toes!!  I would take a poster too... but i dont think that Pontiac would care about the above posters i posted so i would take one of them... As for one of my car... i need to get good pics first! lol!<P>MinnGreen.. still waiting for those cd's... gonna go down and check the mail box now!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>------------------<BR>          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">          <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">     <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">      <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Fastback, Black and Yellow Interior, Planning 4G63 Turbo DSM swap for it!</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
Z||000039||chester||12-25-2001||11:21 AM||||Hi everyone,<P>For those that just want a large print of your car you can send a high resolution image via e-mail to a company called zip marketing ( <A HREF="http://www.zipmarketing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.zipmarketing.com</A>  ) and they can make you a print to whatever size you want.  I had this poster done about a year and a half ago and it has held up well. They will use UV resistant dyes if you so request. Just an FYI for those of you who want a one off of their car.  Ordering was painless and the poster was mailed to me by second day air!<P>Rob D.<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/poster.JPG">   <P>Think its time to update my poster   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">       <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000040||Denny||12-25-2001||12:02 PM||||This will give everyone an idea of grgoyl86's (and mine!) capabilities.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/se_poster.jpg"> <P>I assembled the collage (need a new one, car is highly custom now!), Bob printed it. This was an early attempt and a pretty good one. Bob has a similar one of his car. <P>Anyone who attended Carlisle in May may remember the poster on display at our tent.  Same deal there, I assembled, Bob printed. Bob and I have some pretty sophisticated software. Anyone interested please contact either of us. We are not looking to make a lot of money on this, mostly to recover costs.||||reg||1
Z||000041||FieroMontreal||12-25-2001||12:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Denny:<BR><B>This will give everyone an idea of grgoyl86's (and mine!) capabilities.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/se_poster.jpg">  <P>I assembled the collage (need a new one, car is highly custom now!), Bob printed it. This was an early attempt and a pretty good one. Bob has a similar one of his car. <P>Anyone who attended Carlisle in May may remember the poster on display at our tent.  Same deal there, I assembled, Bob printed. Bob and I have some pretty sophisticated software. Anyone interested please contact either of us. We are not looking to make a lot of money on this, mostly to recover costs.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>ok well I love that. How much would it be to make something like that?<BR>Thanks<BR>Alex<BR><P>------------------<BR> -Alex <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontrealholidays.gif"> <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000042||MinnGreenGT||12-26-2001||09:45 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by chester:<BR><B>Hi everyone,<P>For those that just want a large print of your car you can send a high resolution image via e-mail to a company called zip marketing ( <A HREF="http://www.zipmarketing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.zipmarketing.com</A>  ) and they can make you a print to whatever size you want.  I had this poster done about a year and a half ago and it has held up well. They will use UV resistant dyes if you so request. Just an FYI for those of you who want a one off of their car.  Ordering was painless and the poster was mailed to me by second day air!<P>Rob D.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It's a good poster, but why would you want to send to an "outside company" when you could buy from grgoyl86 or myself? You know... supporting PFF members kinda thing?  I understand of course that you had this done prior to any PFF members discussing/announcing this... I'm just not sure it's necessary to promote another company.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Just my thoughts.<P>Denny & grgoyl86 -looks good.  What kind of machine are you guys using anyway?<P>For those that haven't seen this pic (it's shown up in few threads...) This is my car at Fierorama last fall & the display I printed & created for show use.  The display is 2'x3' and is self supporting... and it stayed out during the entire time it rained (face down in the water some of the time) and the graphic is still like new.  <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/greendisplay1.jpg"> <BR>The frame is normally sold for $95, but I'd be willing to sell them for less to PFF members if anyone is interested... like $50 (+shipping).||||reg||1
Z||000043||chester||12-26-2001||01:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR>[B] It's a good poster, but why would you want to send to an "outside company" when you could buy from grgoyl86 or myself? You know... supporting PFF members kinda thing?  I understand of course that you had this done prior to any PFF members discussing/announcing this... I'm just not sure it's necessary to promote another company.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Just my thoughts.<BR>B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmm, I simply passed along another source for getting the same thing done. Just passing along some knowledge and experience FOR FREE.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">       <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||1
Z||000044||MinnGreenGT||12-26-2001||02:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by chester:<BR><B> Hmmm, I simply passed along another source for getting the same thing done. Just passing along some knowledge and experience FOR FREE.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>OK.  <P>Sorry if I seemed a bit harsh... business has been completely in the dumps since 9/11 (the market basically evaporated a month after we started our company) and work has been a touchy subject. So I'm cutting my margins just simply trying to get some market stimulation here.  I just didn't want to see potential Fiero business go elsewhere.<P>BTW: I recall that you bought pherder's APC Drag Wing... have you gotten around to installing it yet? I'm quite interested to see what it looks like on a fastback!||||reg||1
Z||000045||chester||12-26-2001||02:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by MinnGreenGT:<BR><B> OK.  <P>Sorry if I seemed a bit harsh... business has been completely in the dumps since 9/11 (the market basically evaporated a month after we started our company) and work has been a touchy subject. So I'm cutting my margins just simply trying to get some market stimulation here.  I just didn't want to see potential Fiero business go elsewhere.<P>BTW: I recall that you bought pherder's APC Drag Wing... have you gotten around to installing it yet? I'm quite interested to see what it looks like on a fastback!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry to hear about the business thing.  I know it was an impact on everyone.  Yes I did buy the wing from pherder only problem is that the damn mail system is holding it hostage.  Going on 3 weeks on a priority package.  I've been checking my mail daily and no package  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Hopefully it will make it here and we don't have to go thru the postal insurance thing.  I'll post pics as soon as I get it and install. <P><BR>Rob D.<P>||||reg||1
